<title>NORWAY: POLL-Norske Skog H1 profits seen plunging.</title>
<headline>POLL-Norske Skog H1 profits seen plunging.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norske Skog, Norway's biggest forestry group, is expected to post sharply lower pre-tax profits of 270 million crowns in the first half of 1997, according to a consensus forecast by eight analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>The corresponding year-ago profit was 1.04 billion crowns.</p>
<p>However, sentiments are still positive although Norske's share has gone up almost 25 percent since the first-quarter results were announced. Four analysts said buy, three sold hold. Only one recommended to sell Norske Skog stock.</p>
<p>Norske Skog will present the first-half result at 0600 GMT on August 21.</p>
